WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.200
Last time, a real page beat the model.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.200
It answered on thirty-nine of those words.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.600
So find those words before asking.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.300
Score each line. Keep the best window.

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.300
The first window was the FAQ.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.800
It has more prices. None is a plan.

7
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.600
Words cannot tell them apart. Shape can.

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.100
Near a heading, and not a question.

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.500
Then the heading was wrong. Twice.

10
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.900
A page title, and then a subtitle.

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.400
The same page now answers correctly.

12
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.200
And a second company, with a free plan.

13
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.800
It had also been pricing a docs page.

14
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.500
Discovery already knew. Now we ask it.

15
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.700
One thing is still wrong, and it is the type.

16
00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.600
Three bugs. All found by running it.
